notes.body:
> The proprietary hardware tool is a sniffer that gathers the packet information from the network and passes it to Wireshark using the pcap format.

What link-layer type value does it use?

Either:

- it uses one of the `LINKTYPE_USER`''n'' types;
- it is improperly using some other type;

as there is currently no `LINKTYPE_` value assigned to G.9903.

If it's the former, there is no need for new `WTAP_ENCAP_` values - those `LINKTYPE_` values already *have* `WTAP_ENCAP_` values assigned to them.

If it's the latter, they need to stop ***right now***.  Either:

- the values they chose are in the ranges 0-11, 50-51, 99, 100-146 or 163-292, in which case they have chosen a value *already assigned to some other purpose*, and Wireshark either *already* dissect it as something else or it may do so at some point in the future;
- the values they chose are in the range 147-162, in which case they've chosen one of the `LINKTYPE_USER`''n'' types;
- the values they chose are above 162, in which case they are not *yet* assigned to some other purpose, and may get assigned in some other purpose in the future, and dissected by Wireshark as something else;
- the values they chose are less than 100 and not one of the values listed above, in which case it may end up being dissected as something else on other platforms.

If they've chose a value already assigned to some other purpose, we do not, and will not, guarantee that we do not already dissect it as something other than G.9903 or that we won't dissect it as something other than G.9903 in the future, and they should either:

- switch to using a `LINKTYPE_USER`''n'' type, which will always remain a `LINKTYPE_USER`''n'' type, but which the user might have configured to be dissected as something else;
- request, by sending a message to tcpdump-workers@lists.tcpdump.org, that two LINKTYPE_ values be assigned for the two flavors of G3 - ***note well that this will require that they provide a detailed public specification for the format of the packets, including whatever metadata header they place before the 802.15.4 header***;
- request that two values be reserved - this is *only* if they *insist* on keeping the packet format private, and we (the pcap/pcapng link-layer type managers) would *really* prefer that they not do that.

